INVALID. Do not read a score off this run. The harness said so itself, and it is right.

    +67 =127 -46 over 240 games, score 54.375% on 120 pairs in 35 clusters
    terminations: both_failed 23, init 2, checkmate 111, threefold_repetition 71,
                  fifty_moves 27, insufficient_material 5, stalemate 1

Twenty-five games of 240, 10.4%, were decided by an agent failing to import inside the
platform's 90 second budget rather than by chess. `both_failed` is both agents timing out
at once, which the referee scores void, and a void pair scores 1.0/2, so every one of them
is a forced draw sitting in the number above.

Cause, measured rather than guessed: five workers means ten agent processes, and each one
spends its first minute compiling numba kernels. The machine was not idle while this ran.
Rocket League was using 7.8 GB and Brave, Steam, Discord and another agent session most of
the rest, leaving about 7 GB free, and the import that takes 65 s alone takes longer than
90 s when ten of them compile against that. The previous handoff recorded the same failure
mode and the same cause.

The failures are symmetric, so they do not favour either side; they dilute whatever the real
difference is towards 50%. That means the true figure is more likely above 54.375% than
below it. It does not mean 54.375% may be reported, and it is not reported.

Re-run at three workers, which is the setting that played 120 games in `match-pilot-kb4-vs-kb1`
with no failure at all, on the same opening half, at the same control, with the length
declared before the start and not extended afterwards.
